","code":".data"},{"text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Refreshing without losing data","type":"heading","anchor":"Refreshing-without-losing-data","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"text":" always shows ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":" first, which is right for the initial fetch but wrong for pull-to-refresh — the list shouldn’t disappear behind a spinner while it’s being refetched. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection(_:)"},{"text":" instead: it keeps the current ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" on screen while the operation runs, and leaves it there if the operation fails instead of switching to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["List(articles) { article in","    Text(article.title)","}",".refreshable {","    await store.refreshCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":" for the duration; a failure is reported via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.refreshError"},{"text":" rather than by discarding ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":", so the list stays visible and you can surface the error separately (a toast, for example)."}]},{"text":"Retrying on failure","type":"heading","anchor":"Retrying-on-failure","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a flaky call worth retrying 